From 603e7330df36f3ec927d59ab8e181bf19354ae73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:27:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] driver: forward GCC's -s to the linker

`-s` was accepted with "tolerated but not implemented", so
`lccc -g -s` kept every .debug_* section and .symtab on all four
targets. GCC's -s means only "strip at link time": it passes -s to
the linker, and lccc-ld and every builtin linker already parse it
(linker_common/args.rs). Forward it in command-line order, like
-rdynamic.

Measured with t.c (-g): lccc, lccc-arm, lccc-riscv and lccc-i686
before: 3 .debug_* sections and .symtab, plus the warning; after: no
.debug_* section, no .symtab, no warning.
