From 2331b7f126cf2d5824bc69ed5bad6f9ba4932f37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:30:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] linker: AArch64 section-table audit fixes and TLS across
 DSOs

Section tables (follow-up to the AArch64 DWARF/.symtab commit):
- shdr: section_of() keeps every in-image address section-relative
  (the nearest section before it), so a symbol in a dropped empty
  section never becomes SHN_ABS -- ld.so and gdb do not relocate an
  absolute symbol; header_index() maps a name to its header index.
- merge: the debug-section merge and placement are generic
  (place_debug_sections), shared with the RISC-V linker.
- TLS .symtab values are template offsets, .tbss follows .tdata,
  .rela.plt carries SHF_INFO_LINK, hidden globals keep st_other,
  static IFUNC stubs are named .plt, as in bfd.

TLS (each case was silently wrong or refused):
- TLSDESC->LE wrote the TP offset's low half into the resolver
  register (the LDR's Rt, x1) instead of x0: wrong values in every
  executable linked from -fPIC objects using TLS.
- GD->LE left `bl __tls_get_addr; nop`; it becomes
  `mrs x1, tpidr_el0; add x0, x1, x0`, the CALL26 is skipped and
  gets no PLT entry.
- A TLS variable imported from a DSO got a GLOB_DAT GOT slot; it is
  now R_AARCH64_TLS_TPREL64, and descriptor/GD access to an import
  is relaxed to IE through that slot, as GNU ld does.
- Shared objects support IE, GD and TLSDESC (tls_got.rs): TPREL64,
  DTPMOD64/DTPREL64 and eager R_AARCH64_TLSDESC, by name when
  preemptible, else against the object with the template offset.
  Local-exec relocations are refused as in GNU ld.
- Exported TLS .dynsym values are template offsets (they were
  absolute: importers read outside the module's TLS block) and
  st_shndx names the real section instead of 1.

Validated by tests/linker tls_shared_matrix (x86-64, i686, AArch64,
RISC-V under qemu; 172 links; baseline 47 pass / 82 fail) and the
linker suite.
