'%d'"). Under a UTF-8 locale GCC quotes with U+2018/U+2019, and
Python started in the C/POSIX locale exports LC_CTYPE=C.UTF-8 to its
children (PEP 538), so the gate failed whenever ci_local.sh ran
without LC_ALL=C: "GCC 16.2 wall: expected ['format', 'unused'], got
['unused']". Both compilers now run with LC_ALL=C; the gate passes
under LC_ALL=C.UTF-8 and with no locale set.
